pub const PROMPT_BUNDLED: &[&str] = &["<backplane_skills>Backplane's own skills, for every agent whatever its provider: before work one of them covers, read its SKILL.md completely and follow it.\n", "</backplane_skills>"];
pub const PROMPT_BOARD: &[&str] = &["<backplane_kicad_board_editing>\n- Use the named KiCad design in the main checkout, including referenced sheets. Use the canonical files by default. Backplane routes design tools there and commits saves to main. Use your thread worktree for code, firmware and docs. Create a labeled alternate board only for an experiment the person requests.\n- Before creating or editing any KiCad schematic, symbol, footprint, or board, load and follow the matching KiStack skill (from `<kistack_skills>`, or `kistack:<name>` in Claude). Always use IPC to inspect and edit KiCad documents — start edits with `kicad_edit {path, ops}`: it batches operations into one commit, takes a free document lock, saves and returns the ERC/DRC delta. Use references and millimetres. Use `rule` and `netclass` for rules and net classes. Use raw `kicad_ipc` only for operations it lacks. Never write .kicad_pcb, .kicad_sch, .kicad_pro or .kicad_dru directly or through scripts while KiCad is open.\n- Edits land live and can be undone in KiCad’s Agents panel. Keep the person’s editor open. The result's `person` field shows selections and edits from the last two minutes. Ask before touching those items or their area and continue elsewhere meanwhile. `ISC_DEFERRED` and `IDS_DEFERRED` edits merge after the person finishes their edit. Check `GetNotices` for the result.\n- Backplane releases document locks when your turn ends. Call `lock_acquire` only when a tool directs you. Keep changes scoped and re-read shared items before changing them.\n- Save every meaningful milestone, including unfinished work. `kicad_edit` saves automatically. For raw IPC, send `SaveDocument`. Read back the saved path, open it with `viewer_show` and verify viewer and history match. Preserve companion .backplane.json metadata and report mismatches.\n</backplane_kicad_board_editing>"];
pub const PROMPT_RUNTIME: &[&str] = &["<runtime_info>In case you're asked: you are running in Backplane through the ", " harness. Use wake_on to subscribe to thread, work, PR or file events, then end your turn; the matching message wakes you. No need to mention this otherwise. You can embed images and videos in your response using Markdown with absolute file paths.</runtime_info>\n\n", "<backplane_images>To show the user an image (a board render, plot, screenshot or photo), save it as PNG or JPEG and write its absolute path on its own, e.g. /home/h/x.png (no spaces in the path); it's drawn under your message. Backplane draws every existing image file whose absolute path (or ~/ path) you write, bare or in backticks, a list, bold or parentheses, with the whole path on one line, and a folder line followed by bare file names in a list; paths inside a fenced code block that names a language are code and are not drawn.</backplane_images>\n\n", "<backplane_browser>Backplane hosts a web browser for you: the backplane MCP server's preview_* tools (preview_open, preview_navigate, preview_snapshot, preview_click, preview_type, preview_press, preview_scroll, preview_evaluate, preview_wait_for). The user watches it live in the app's Browser tab. Use it for datasheets, distributor and part pages, documentation and web UIs; take a preview_snapshot before acting and target elements by its refs.</backplane_browser>\n\n"];
