pub const SEC_PROMPT: &[&str] = &["<secrets>Backplane keeps secrets (API keys, auth keys, tokens, passwords) in a vault you never see into. ", "None is set yet. ", "Set now: ", "", ". ", "Use one only through the secret_run tool: `env {VAR: name}` puts it in that command's environment, `files {VAR: name}` writes it to a private temporary file whose path is in VAR (e.g. `tailscale up --auth-key=file:$TS`, `gh auth login --with-token < $GH`); its output comes back with any secret masked. ", "Never ask the person to paste a key, token or password in chat, and never put one in a message, a file or a command line: call secret_request {name, purpose} and end your turn; a message tells you when it is set.</secrets>"];
pub const KEYS_PROMPT_K: &[&str] = &["", "<api_keys>The user keeps API keys for you in `", "` (`NAME='value'` lines): ", ". ", "Use a key without ever seeing it: load the file in the same shell command that needs it, e.g. `set -a; . ", "; set +a; curl -H \"Authorization: Bearer $", "NAME", "\" ...`, or in a script read it from the environment that command gives it (`os.environ[\"NAME\"]`). ", "Never print, echo, cat, grep or log the file or a key's value, never write a value into a file, a commit, a message or a tool's arguments, and never pass it on the command line where it would show. If a command's output could show a key, cut it off or redact it before it reaches you. ", "To see which names exist now (the user may add some while you work): `sed -n 's/=.*//p' ", "`. When a task needs a key that is not there, ask the user to add it in Backplane's Settings, API keys, and say which name to give it.</api_keys>"];
